		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD-UV390 has 417Hz tone during Tx]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5212&amp;p=37719#p37719"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Another club member has been digging into the problem.  It seems that the tone we hear is likely a harmonic of the CTCSS tone for the repeater.  Interestingly, during a net this morning, my friend monitored with his test equipment and noticed the tone was present on everyone's Tx, although it wasn't audible.  I've tried boosting my mic gain to see if that resolves it but it does not.<br><br>BTW, recording of the uplink from my radio does not have the tone.<br><br>So it seems part of the problem is our local repeater but the issue is definitely aggravated by something in the OGD77 FW in my TYT MD-UV390.  Bottom line:  I can live with this as I like the additional capabilities OGD77 brings to the radio (it's the reason I picked up the radio in the first place).  This seems to be the only repeater in our area where I have this issue, so I'll just not use the TYT on that repeater.<br><br>It is a mystery though.  I'll post if further testing turns up any additional information.<br><br>Steve</div></blockquote>As your friend to measure the deviation of the CTCSS tone on you radio and other people's radios.<br><br>My guess is that the deviation of the tone on OpenGD77 may be slightly higher, however reducing the deviation used by the firmware would not be practical as it my prevent some people accessing repeaters which need this much deviation<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Jul 15, 2025 8:51 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
