		<title type="html"><![CDATA[MD-UV390 has 417Hz tone during Tx]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5212&amp;p=37705#p37705"><![CDATA[
I'm running the 20241215 FW, but this also occurred using the 20240908 FW.  Whenever I contact someone using a local repeater at 146.73, my Tx transmissions have a 417Hz tone in the background.  This has nothing to do with my location as it occurs from home or when I am participating in a net from a local park.  In the latter case, there are other Hams with me using other radios and they don't have the tone on their signals.  When I use any other radio from either location, there is no tone.<br><br>Today, I reverted to the OEM FW, and the tone was not present.  When I reloaded OGD77 upgrading to FW 20241215, the tone returned.  I've checked the channel settings and I see no settings that might cause this.  The channel is set to the proper upload PL tone.  This does not happen when I use Simplex at 146.000 or on another repeater at 146.07.<br><br>I forgot to mention I have an MD-UV390 GPS.  Another clue is that someone else I know has the MD-UV390 plus and gets the same tone on the same repeater during Tx.<br><br>Any clues on why apparently one repeater is doing this and not another or on simplex??<br><br>Steve W3ATN<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5794">W3ATN</a> — Sat Jul 12, 2025 7:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
